    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0079" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg39"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 832.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">
                                December</hi> 16, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>In accordance with the desire expressed in 1164, of the 29th of November, I have
                    transmitted to Lord Russell the information contained in General Dix’s letter
                    respecting the rebel organization at Marysburg, Prince Edward’s county, in
                    Canada.</p>
                <p>It is announced that Parliament will meet for the despatch of business on the 7th
                    of February next.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p> Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
